  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0303' consists of six tables: Project, Acceptance_Criteria_Table, Sprint, Message_Event, Story, and Task.\nThe Project table is used to store information about the projects. It includes columns for creation_time, project_ID (as the primary key), project_description, project_name, and update_time.\nThe Acceptance_Criteria_Table stores details about the acceptance criteria for each project. It includes columns for acceptance_criteria_ID, description, and status.\nThe Sprint table contains information about each sprint, including end_time, project_ID (as a foreign key referencing the Project table), sprint_ID (as the primary key), sprint_name, start_time, and status.\nThe Message_Event table stores information about messages and events related to each project. It includes columns for creation_time, message_event_ID (as the primary key), message_reference, project_ID (as a foreign key referencing the Project table), subject, update_time, and version.\nThe Story table contains details about each story related to a project and sprint. It includes columns for description, project_ID (as a foreign key referencing the Project table), sprint_ID (as a foreign key referencing the Sprint table), status, story_ID (as the primary key), story_points, and title.\nFinally, the Task table stores information about tasks related to each story. It includes columns for description, status, story_ID (as a foreign key referencing the Story table), task_ID (as the primary key), and title.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements Description:\nThis database is for an Agile Development Management System used to manage stories (requirements), tasks, sprints (iterations), and acceptance criteria within a project. The primary features include:\n1.Manage Stories (Requirements): Create and edit stories, including story descriptions, status, story points, and titles. Assign stories to specific projects and sprints.\n2.Manage Tasks: For each story, create and assign tasks, including task titles, descriptions, and status.\n3.Manage Sprints (Iterations): Create and manage sprints within a project. Each sprint belongs to a project and includes a name, start time, end time, and status. Assign stories to specific sprints.\n4.Manage Acceptance Criteria: For each story, create acceptance criteria, including criteria ID, description, and status. Track and manage the acceptance criteria for stories.\n5.Message Event Management: Record message events related to specific topics, including event ID, subject, message reference, version, creation time, and update time. This is used for messaging and event recording within the project.\nThrough these features, the system helps teams better manage and track project progress, ensuring each story and task is completed on time and meets the acceptance criteria.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0303.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0303\nCREATE TABLE `Project` (\n  `project_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `project_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`project_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Acceptance_Criteria_Table` (\n  `acceptance_criteria_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`acceptance_criteria_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Sprint` (\n  `sprint_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sprint_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `project_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sprint_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sprint_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_ID`) REFERENCES `Project` (`project_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Message_Event` (\n  `message_event_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `subject` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `message_reference` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `version` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `project_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`message_event_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `message_event_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_ID`) REFERENCES `Project` (`project_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Story` (\n  `story_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `story_points` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `project_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sprint_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`story_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `story_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_ID`) REFERENCES `Project` (`project_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `story_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`sprint_ID`) REFERENCES `Sprint` (`sprint_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Task` (\n  `task_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `story_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`task_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `task_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`story_ID`) REFERENCES `Story` (`story_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
